From: Wasmer Engineering <engineering@wasmer.io>
Subject: [PATCH] Allow static wee8 builds to use the dynamic Windows CRT

Rust's Windows MSVC targets use the dynamic CRT by default. Allow wee8 to
match that runtime without enabling component builds (wee8 remains a static
library). Apply the choice to release_crt as well for consistency.

The embedder must also disable the allocator shim and PartitionAlloc's
malloc replacement when selecting this mode.

diff --git a/build/config/win/BUILD.gn b/build/config/win/BUILD.gn
--- a/build/config/win/BUILD.gn
+++ b/build/config/win/BUILD.gn
@@ -527,10 +527,15 @@
 # CRT --------------------------------------------------------------------------
 
+declare_args() {
+  # Use the embedder's DLL CRT even when wee8 itself is a static library.
+  wee8_use_dynamic_crt = false
+}
+
 # Configures how the runtime library (CRT) is going to be used.
 # See https://msdn.microsoft.com/en-us/library/2kzt1wy3.aspx for a reference of
 # what each value does.
 config("default_crt") {
-  if (is_component_build) {
+  if (is_component_build || wee8_use_dynamic_crt) {
     # Component mode: dynamic CRT. Since the library is shared, it requires
     # exceptions or will give errors about things not matching, so keep
     # exceptions on.
@@ -553,8 +558,8 @@
 # tools that need to be fully optimized even in debug builds, for those times
 # when the debug CRT is part of the bottleneck. This also avoids *implicitly*
 # defining _DEBUG.
 config("release_crt") {
-  if (is_component_build) {
+  if (is_component_build || wee8_use_dynamic_crt) {
     cflags = [ "/MD" ]
 
     # /MD specifies msvcrt.lib as the CRT library, which is the dynamic+release
